/* ================================================================= */
/* HOW THIS FILE IS ORGANISED                                        */
/* ----------------------------------------------------------------- */
/*                                                                   */
/* SELECTOR PREFIX                                                   */
/*   Nearly every rule starts `html body.obsidian-app` so it beats   */
/*   Obsidian without !important. Keep it. The few unprefixed rules  */
/*   target chrome outside .obsidian-app (titlebar) or deliberately  */
/*   want the lower specificity.                                     */
/*                                                                   */
/* TOKENS - change these, not the values below                       */
/*   --aubade-thickness       every border width                     */
/*   --aubade-divider-color   every border and divider colour        */
/*   --aubade-pattern-color   what the header patterns draw in       */
/*   --button-shadow-offset   the offset drop shadow                 */
/*   --button-lift / -press   hover and active displacement          */
/*   --aubade-callout-*       callout hues, tint, title plate        */
/*   All live in 01. Presets (32) override only the raw palette      */
/*   declared in 02 and 03.                                          */
/*                                                                   */
/* CASCADE - rule order is load-bearing                              */
/*   Two rules of equal specificity touching the same property       */
/*   resolve by which comes last. Add new rules at the end of their  */
/*   section; do not reorder existing ones without re-testing.       */
/*                                                                   */
/*   !important is kept to a verified minimum: 57 remain, down from  */
/*   230. Each was tested by removing it in a live vault and diffing */
/*   the computed styles of every element; each one changed the      */
/*   rendering, or covers a surface that could not be reached.       */
/*                                                                   */
/*   Toggles (.checkbox-container) need it on EVERY declaration.     */
/*   Obsidian scopes its own toggle rules under .modal, giving them  */
/*   (0,3,1) against this file's (0,2,3) - class count wins, so the  */
/*   prefix loses. Strip them and the thumb slides out of the track. */
/*                                                                   */
/*   When testing, remember the settings window is a SEPARATE        */
/*   document. Anything Obsidian scopes under .modal only shows its  */
/*   true cascade there, not in the main window.                     */
/*                                                                   */
/* PLATFORM GATES                                                    */
/*   .is-mobile             phone and tablet     -> 20               */
/*   :not(.is-mobile)       desktop only                             */
/*   @media (hover: hover)  pointer devices, so touch never sticks   */
/*                                                                   */
/* STYLE SETTINGS CLASSES                                            */
/*   preset-*      colour scheme      -> 32                          */
/*   pattern-*     titlebar pattern   -> 24                          */
/*   hide-ribbon   autohide ribbon    -> 29                          */
/*   show-tooltips                    -> 14                          */
/*   expand-all-longtext              -> 29                          */
/*                                                                   */
/* NOTE CSSCLASSES (opt in per note via frontmatter)                 */
/*   dashboard, hide-all        -> 23                                */
/*   custom-timeline            -> 30, 31                            */
/*   width-800 ... full-width   -> 18                                */
/*                                                                   */
/* NAVIGATION - three heading levels, each greppable                 */
/*   1 Section      NN. TITLE inside a full-width == box, with a     */
/*                  summary and a See-also cross-reference.          */
/*                  grep -n "^/\* [0-9][0-9]\."  theme.css           */
/*   2 Sub-section  a -- Title -- bar sitting between rules.         */
/*                  grep -n "^/\* -- "  theme.css                    */
